# Architecture

Declarative VS Code language extension. No server, DB, HTTP API, bundler or webview. Details: `docs/architecture.md`.

- **Data** `data/risingwave.json` is the single source of truth (keywords, connectors, docs). Model: `docs/db/README.md`.
- **Build** `scripts/build.js` regenerates grammar `generated:*` regexes and `GEN:*` sections in `README.md` / `SKILL.md`. `npm run check` detects drift.
- **Runtime** `extension.js` (only `vscode` imports) registers file badge, hover, completion. Logic lives in `lib/keywords.js`.
- **Static assets** grammar, snippets, theme, icon theme are wired in `package.json` → `contributes`. Contract: `docs/api.md`.

# Design

- Hover: longest compound keyword containing the cursor wins; falls back to the single word. Compound keywords match per line only.
- Completion is context-free by design (full list every time).
- Option keys (`type`, `connector`, …) and `JSON`/`AVRO` values highlight only in context (`WITH ( )`, after `ENCODE`/`FORMAT`).
- Scope naming `<category>.<sub>.<dialect>.<role>`; orange = RisingWave, Dark+ colours = PostgreSQL. Every new scope needs a theme rule. Tokens: `docs/frontend.md`.

# Functionality

Highlighting, hover (26 docs), completion, 35 snippets, `RW` badge, icon theme, dark theme. Checklist with module pointers: `docs/features.md`. Flows: `docs/user-flows.md`.

# Principles

- Edit data/snippets, then `npm run build`; never hand-edit generated regions.
- Keep `extension.js` thin; test via `lib/` and `test/grammar.test.js`.
- `npm run verify` before commit. Record major changes in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Known gaps and open findings: `docs/audit.md`.
